      "text": "Recorded my assessment as of event 23 (t = 2880 s): the run looks normal so far, and there's no sample data yet to say whether the material grew.\n\n- **Purge:** oxygen in the exhaust dropped from 28,765 ppm to about 5 ppm and has stayed there since.\n- **Heating:** the thermocouple followed the ramp setpoint closely. It overshot to 760.8 °C when the growth hold began and settled to 750.0 °C.\n- **Gas and pressure:** argon flow matches the 100 sccm setpoint, and tube pressure is steady at about 3.02–3.06 Torr.\n- **Heater power:** it fell from about 84% to 41–46% at the hold. That's expected once the furnace stops ramping, but no reference values from normal runs came with these events, so I couldn't compare it against them.\n\nI recommended continuing; nothing points to a fault. The result will only count as evidence about the recipe once the sample is characterized after growth."
